{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And his master shall bore through.</b> And why with an awl? Because מרצע in gematria is four hundred. Said the Holy One, blessed be He: I took you out from four hundred years of servitude, and I said, ״כי לי בני ישראל עבדים״ — and he went and acquired a master for himself; therefore he is struck with the awl." "<b>And he shall serve him forever.</b> Until the olam of Levi, which is the Jubilee, fifty years. And it is written regarding Samuel, who was a Levite: ״וישב שם עד עולם״, and Samuel lived fifty-two years, and he was two years old when his mother brought him to the House of HaShem — if so, his lifelong dwelling was fifty years."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:36.322001850Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}